abstract = {Conversation analysis is the term used to refer to the study of talk in interaction. It seeks to discover and describe the normative structures and practices that make interaction possible and intelligible and the ways in which participants use these resources to perform and coordinate activities, i.e. social actions, in talk. Conversational analysis has shown powerfully that talk is a highly organised phenomenon whose orderliness allows for participants' understandings of one another's conduct. This issue of "Nottingham French Studies" presents a collection of conversation-analytic and interactional-linguistic studies on the French language to showcase current and ongoing research in French conversational analysis.},
